\section{Magnetic flux}

For a uniform field $B$ through a flat area $A$,
\[
\Phi = B A \cos\theta,
\]
where $\theta$ is the angle between $\vec B$ and the \textbf{normal} to the area.
\begin{itemize}
  \item $B\perp$ area ($\theta=0$): $\Phi=BA$ (maximum).
  \item $B\parallel$ area ($\theta=90^\circ$): $\Phi=0$.
  \item Unit: \textbf{weber} (Wb). $1\,\mathrm{Wb}=1\,\mathrm{T\,m^{2}}$.
  \item Coil of $N$ turns: \textbf{flux linkage} $=N\Phi$.
\end{itemize}

