\section{Faraday's law and Lenz's law}

\subsection{Faraday's law}
The magnitude of the induced e.m.f.\ equals the rate of change of flux linkage:
\[
\mathcal{E} = N\,\frac{|\Delta\Phi|}{\Delta t}
\qquad\text{or}\qquad
\mathcal{E} = -N\,\frac{\mathrm{d}\Phi}{\mathrm{d}t}.
\]
The minus sign encodes Lenz's law.

\subsection{Lenz's law}
The induced current flows in the direction that \textbf{opposes the change} that produced it.

