\subsection{Fleming's right-hand rule (generator rule)}
For a conductor moving in $\vec B$:
\begin{itemize}
  \item thu\textbf{M}b --- Motion
  \item \textbf{F}irst finger --- Field $B$
  \item se\textbf{C}ond finger --- induced Current $I$
\end{itemize}
(Left hand $=$ motor / force; right hand $=$ generator / induced current.)

\ex
A 1-turn circular coil of radius $10\,\mathrm{cm}$ sits perpendicular to a uniform field.
$B$ decreases at $0.02\,\mathrm{T\,s^{-1}}$.
\begin{enumerate}
  \item State the direction of the induced current (viewed so $\vec B$ is into the page and decreasing).
  \item Find the magnitude of the induced e.m.f.
\end{enumerate}

\sol
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Into-page flux is decreasing. Lenz: induced current tries to \textbf{maintain}
        into-page flux $\Rightarrow$ current clockwise (RH grip: thumb into page).
  \item $|\mathcal{E}|=A\,\bigl|\Delta B/\Delta t\bigr|
        =\pi(0.10)^{2}(0.02)=6.3\times 10^{-4}\,\mathrm{V}$.
\end{enumerate}

\ex
A flat coil has $N=200$ turns and area $A=1.5\times 10^{-3}\,\mathrm{m^{2}}$.
Uniform $B$ rises from $0.20\,\mathrm{T}$ to $0.50\,\mathrm{T}$ in $0.10\,\mathrm{s}$.
Coil resistance $R=4.0\,\Omega$.
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Find the average induced e.m.f.
  \item Find the average induced current if the coil is closed through $R$.
\end{enumerate}

\sol
\begin{enumerate}
  \item $|\Delta\Phi|=A\Delta B=(1.5\times 10^{-3})(0.30)=4.5\times 10^{-4}\,\mathrm{Wb}$.
        $\mathcal{E}=N|\Delta\Phi|/\Delta t
        =200\times(4.5\times 10^{-4})/0.10=0.90\,\mathrm{V}$.
  \item $I=\mathcal{E}/R=0.90/4.0=0.225\,\mathrm{A}$.
\end{enumerate}

%======================================================================
\section{Motional e.m.f.}

A conducting rod of length $\ell$ moving at speed $v$ perpendicular to a uniform
field $B$ (and to its own length) has induced e.m.f.
\[
\mathcal{E} = B\ell v.
\]
Charges in the rod feel $F=qvB$ until $qE=qvB$ balances; ends become charged.
If the rod slides on closed rails, a current $I=\mathcal{E}/R$ flows.

