%======================================================================
\section{Simple generators}

A coil rotating in a magnetic field has changing flux linkage
$\Rightarrow$ alternating induced e.m.f.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lll@{}}
\toprule
 & a.c.\ generator & d.c.\ generator \\
\midrule
Connections & \textbf{slip rings} & \textbf{commutator} \\
Output & reverses each half-turn & same direction in external circuit \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\begin{itemize}
  \item Replace slip rings by a commutator $\Rightarrow$ a.c.\ generator becomes a d.c.\ generator.
  \item Commutator reverses coil-to-circuit connections every half-turn so the
        external current stays one way (still varying in size --- ``unsteady d.c.'').
\end{itemize}

Ways to increase induced e.m.f.: more turns, stronger $B$, larger coil area,
soft-iron core, higher rotation speed.

\worked{2022}{28}{D}{}{../2022_q28.png}{%
