\section{Practice questions}

\subsection*{Typed practice}
\ex
A square loop of side $6.0\,\mathrm{cm}$ ($N=1$) moves at $v=5.0\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$
into a uniform field $B=0.80\,\mathrm{T}$ perpendicular to the loop plane.
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Find the average induced e.m.f.\ while the loop is entering.
  \item How long does entry take?
  \item Once the loop is wholly inside and still moving at constant $v$, what is $\mathcal{E}$?
\end{enumerate}

\sol
\begin{enumerate}
  \item $|\Delta\Phi|=B\ell^{2}=(0.80)(0.060)^{2}=2.88\times 10^{-3}\,\mathrm{Wb}$;
        $\Delta t=\ell/v=0.012\,\mathrm{s}$;
        $\mathcal{E}=|\Delta\Phi|/\Delta t=0.24\,\mathrm{V}$
        (or $\mathcal{E}=B\ell v=0.24\,\mathrm{V}$).
  \item $0.012\,\mathrm{s}$.
  \item $\Phi$ constant $\Rightarrow$ $\mathcal{E}=0$.
\end{enumerate}

\ex
Flux through a single-turn loop changes from $+0.12\,\mathrm{Wb}$ to $-0.12\,\mathrm{Wb}$
in $40\,\mathrm{ms}$. Find the average induced e.m.f.

\sol
$|\Delta\Phi|=0.24\,\mathrm{Wb}$,\quad
$\mathcal{E}=0.24/(0.040)=6.0\,\mathrm{V}$.

\ex
Which change(s) increase the power in a lamp connected to a coil near a moving magnet?
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Insert a soft-iron core into the coil.
  \item Move the magnet faster.
  \item Replace the lamp by one of lower resistance.
\end{enumerate}

\sol
All three: larger $|\Delta\Phi|$ or smaller $\Delta t$ raises $\mathcal{E}$;
lower $R$ raises $I=\mathcal{E}/R$ and $P=I^{2}R$ (for a given $\mathcal{E}$,
lower $R$ still increases current enough that power rises in the usual DSE treatment).
All of (1)(2)(3).

